      ":question/id": "64491ba3-32eb-50b2-9929-829f39d86a6e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Differentiate $-2{e}^{x}\\cos x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=- 2 e^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(x)v(x))' &=u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ &=(- 2 e^{x})'\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(- 2 e^{x})\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ &=(- 2 e^{x})(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(- 2 e^{x})(- \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &=- 2 e^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} \\\\ &\\quad +(2 e^{x} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
